xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:10.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:norma\l;font-family:Arial;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:justify">This entity consists of a card of a card deck, representing the Jack, as if in a common deck of cards, however, the suit of this specific card is shown as the nonexiste\nt suit of Eyes, with an open eye symbol where others like Hearts or Diamonds would be. The Jack itself also has a different appearance from common sets, being shown with an apparently marine type of background on the bottom half, and a sky with clouds on\ the top half. The figure in the center has a distinct aesthetic, not having any hats, or a face, with its head only having many black dots, probably alluding to holes, and on its neck, a collar made of sushi rolls is shown. The color of the suit&#8217;s \numbers and symbols is also different, being yellowish in color. Its origin and context are completely unknown, except for what&#8217;s written on the back of the card, saying: &#8220;Bat: 131.131.119&#8221;. This information can lead to believe that this\ was the batch code for this product, further speculating a possible whole deck in some package, somewhere. When this card is picked up, the one who picked it is marked by its corresponding anomaly, with no warning. While the card is in possession, the an\omaly suddenly appears, in an unknown matter, somewhere close.  When it has its sights on the target \(the one with the card on their hand\) the creature becomes hostile and assigns itself the mission to destroy it at any cost. It doesn&#8217;t appear to \have any personal motivations, only focusing on destroying anyone who has the card, and disappearing when it&#8217;s being owned by no one. After kill confirmation, it leaves, disappearing and leaving no traces</span><span style="font-size:8.0pt;text-alig\n:justify">.</span></p></body>)/Rect[45.3301 40.864 571.332 206.874]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj102 0 obj<</BS 123 0 R/Contents(An element in the shape of an AV-8B Harrier military jet plane, but instead of a pilot seat in its cockpit, a humanoid torso is attached to the rest of the creature. This torso has a biomechanic appearance, but with the upper part being completely organic\, with a faceless head, with a lot of holes on it instead. The torso also appears to be using a headset, with its headphone parts having the form of sushi rolls, and the microphone having the appearance of a transversely skewered nigiri sushi. )/CreationDate(D:-001-1-1-1-1-1-00'30')/DA(0 0 0 rg /Arial 6 Tf)/DS(font: Arial,sans-serif 6.0pt; text-align:left; color:#000000 )/F 4/M(D:20240920154948-03'00')/NM(307836cabaec465cb2dae4cf3ecee1a4)/Page 1/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:24.3.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"  style="font-size:6.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal\;font-family:Arial;font-stretch:normal"><p dir="ltr"><span style="text-align:justify">An element in the shape of an AV-8B Harrier military jet plane, but instead of a pilot seat in its cockpit, a humanoid torso is attached to the rest of the creature. Thi\s torso has a biomechanic appearance, but with the upper part being completely organic, with a faceless head, with a lot of holes on it instead. The torso also appears to be using a headset, with its headphone parts having the form of sushi rolls, and the\ microphone having the appearance of a transversely skewered nigiri sushi. </span></p></body>)/Rect[430.944 257.299 561.643 345.406]/Subj(Text Box)/Subtype/FreeText/T( )/Type/Annot>>endobj103 0 obj<</BS<</W 0>>/CA 1/Contents(   Dif)/DA(0 0 0 RG 0 0 0 rg 0 Tc 0 Tw 100 Tz 0 TL 0 Ts 0 Tr /Helv 21.8 Tf)/DS